Z||000017||1FST2M6||02-14-2000||01:46 PM||||I had an ADS strip chip in my 86 V6 4spd. But after the injector upgrade I had to have it reprogrammed to even start. The ADS chip did make a noticable throttle responce difference and even though the ad says "it won't pass emissions" it does.. just fine. No real fuel economy difference in the stock chip and the ADS unit except my foot seemed heavyier with the new found sense of more go! But like the others have said it's not an instant 10 second stop light monster... but it does help. And every little bit counts.. before you do that, do the cheap things first... Throttle body coolant bypass, intake, CLEAN injectors... etc... ||||reg||1
Z||000018||FIEROCIOUS||02-14-2000||01:55 PM||||I have the ADS chip and have been very happy with it! The biggest differance that I found was that it ran smoother at part throttle than the stock chip! No extra gas consumption, no knocking or pinging. It has a little more umpf up top but not much more.<BR>All in all I'd deffinatly do it again! It only cost me 56.00 well worth the ca$h! I purchased mine from JC whitney.||||reg||1
